I think a fort with a big stack of missile weapons is a fine idea.
Rocks are cheap, too.  But it has some big drawbacks including
wandering giants and hostiles with wands of striking.  Also, you need
to be certain that you can both not be zapped when you enter the level
and get the troll lined up well enough for you to be able to attack it
from range.  It's fraught with peril but certainly feasible with some
clever tactics.  How about trapping the troll with a boulder that you
keep pushing toward it?  A double pit "^^" will also keep the troll
out of an area.  However, you might not have sufficient time for such
"corralling" techniques.  Another problem is that hanging around too
long on Lvl 19 might see the generation of golden nagas or covetous
liches; and that would be bad.

As for the reviving troll: after you kill the troll, it should only
take you 2 moves to push the boulder and autopickup the wand.  If he
revives after 1 move, then he will revive off of the wand anyway with
the boulder on the loot square.

Digging for the castle is a fine idea, but you'll need that wand of
digging to potentially instantly drop through the titan's level.  I've
been surrounded there before by titan storms.  It can happen and it'd
be a shame to kill off a level 14 hero.  Also, be sure that you don't
dig all the way to the castle, take the stairs if possible so that you
don't end up in the middle of the maze with a lich on the upstair and
a minotaur in the maze.  Remember also that Elbereth doesn't protect
against all of the nasties.  If you have a cursed scroll of teleport
you might consider keeping it out of your bag.

